\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O the bitter shame and sorrow,
\par That a time could ever be
\par When I let the Saviour's pity
\par Plead in vain, and proudly answered:
\par All of self, and none of Thee!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Yet He found me. I beheld Him
\par Bleeding on the accursed tree,
\par Heard Him pray: Forgive them, Father!
\par And my wistful heart said faintly:
\par Some of self, and some of Thee!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Day by day His tender mercy,
\par Healing, helper, full and free,
\par Sweet and strong, and, ah! so patient,
\par Brought me lower, while I whispered:
\par Less of self, and more of Thee!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Higher than the highest heaven,
\par Deeper than the deepest sea,
\par Lord, Thy love at last hath conquered;
\par Grant me now my supplication:
\par None of self, and all of Thee!
\par                                   Amen.
\par \f1 
